#: admin/about-tab.php:22
msgid "About Lynbro Danadresse Autofill"
msgstr ""

#: admin/about-tab.php:24
msgid ""
"Danish customers type their address once and pick it from a list. The "
"street, postcode and city land in the right fields, spelled the way the "
"official register spells them — so parcels stop bouncing on a mistyped "
"street name."
msgstr ""

#: admin/about-tab.php:27
msgid ""
"It works on the WooCommerce checkout and on the address field of every major "
"form builder, through adapters that know each plugin's markup. Nothing needs "
"to be wired up by hand."
msgstr ""

#: admin/about-tab.php:32
msgid "How your data is handled"
msgstr ""

#: admin/about-tab.php:34
msgid ""
"Your API key stays on your server. It is stored as a password field, never "
"printed back into a page, and never sent to a visitor's browser."
msgstr ""

#: admin/about-tab.php:35
msgid ""
"Lookups are proxied through your own site, so no visitor IP address is "
"passed on to the address service."
msgstr ""

#: admin/about-tab.php:36
msgid ""
"Responses are cached only for as long as the service says they stay fresh, "
"and never longer."
msgstr ""

#: admin/about-tab.php:37
msgid ""
"The problem log keeps error codes only. Addresses your customers type are "
"never written to your database by this plugin."
msgstr ""

#: admin/about-tab.php:38
msgid ""
"No address data is bundled or downloaded in bulk — every suggestion is a "
"live lookup."
msgstr ""

#: admin/about-tab.php:43
msgid "External service"
msgstr ""

#: admin/about-tab.php:45
msgid ""
"This plugin talks to one service: the danadresse.dk address API "
"(api.danadresse.dk), operated by LynBro ApS, Denmark. It receives the "
"address text being typed — plus, when validation is on, the delivery address "
"of an order — together with your API key, sent from your server. Without a "
"key configured, the plugin makes no external requests at all."
msgstr ""

